"""Section-wise editorial pass; numerical outcomes and native equations preserved."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re
from docx.shared import Pt,Cm
from docx.enum.text import WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH

EDITS=[
('Routing feedback uses airtime,','Missing forwarding evidence can reflect packet loss, contention or an unobserved transmission, making feedback design a joint problem of inference and airtime. We benchmark ACK-gated censored passive feedback against active proofs in 750 IEEE 802.15.4 runs on 30 new fixtures, with naive-passive, frozen-prior and capacity-matched policy controls. Under blackholes, delivery increases from 71.28% to 75.94%, a paired gain of 4.67 percentage points (95% interval 2.36–6.97; Holm-adjusted p=0.0161). Energy per delivered byte falls while total modeled radio energy rises slightly. The controls do not establish a unique censoring or attention advantage. A separate 180-run experiment tests frozen policies over authenticated messages and node-local records. Attention delivers 81.61% in benign conditions and 61.11% under selective dropping, without an established advantage over greedy or multilayer-perceptron routing. Serial-interface testing identifies and corrects a receive-time freshness error. Compiled UART-to-radio firmware runs on four emulated Cortex-M3 boards; neural inference and cryptography execute on the host PC. Each host-policy control delivers ten of ten packets. An exploratory 60–300 s extension exposes routing-energy exhaustion and increasing service debt. The contribution is a traceable comparison of feedback mechanisms and transport boundaries; the evidence does not establish sustained operation, physical-board performance, measured energy consumption or absolute deadline compliance.','Sharpen contribution; distinguish the 750-run feedback benchmark, 180-run transport study and post-review stress evidence.'),
('Our earlier architecture comparisons found','Earlier architecture comparisons found no joint advantage over a multilayer perceptron of similar capacity. A subsequent 600-run telemetry study likewise found no advantage after correction for multiple testing and exposed the traffic cost of active proofs. Both stages and their raw outputs are retained. They motivated the present comparison of receipt-assisted passive feedback with active proofs, subject to prespecified margins against a frozen-prior control on new fixtures.','Replace a rhetorical research question with the concrete experimental contrast.'),
('We compare feedback rules that differ','The technical contribution is a controlled comparison of feedback eligibility, evidence retention and missing-observation handling. Own first-hop ACK success gates credit; an observer–relay–packet record retains its strongest matched observation; missing evidence leaves the effective failure count unchanged. Packet-reception callbacks connect the ledger to simulated radio events. Figures 1 and 2 show the state boundaries and event logic, respectively. The benchmark builds on established watchdog, censoring and learning methods.','State the implemented mechanism before its provenance and figure references.'),
('The benchmark tests blackhole delivery','The prespecified decision combines a blackhole delivery comparison against active proofs with delivery, critical-service and energy-efficiency margins against frozen-prior attention. Naive-passive and capacity-matched controls assess whether the outcome can be attributed specifically to censoring or policy architecture. An improvement over active proofs alone cannot establish either attribution.','Distinguish replacement performance from mechanism or architecture attribution.'),
('The coefficients in Eq. (1) are fixed','Equation (1) uses hand-set preselection coefficients, not learned parameters. The retained source records the values but contains no systematic tuning history. The later ±20% coefficient experiment in Section 5.5 is a local sensitivity check and does not retrospectively optimize this score. Equation (2) divides the query–key product by the square root of 96, as implemented in PyTorch.','Link the heuristic to the actual sensitivity experiment without inventing tuning history.'),
('• g is sinkward','• For observer u and candidate v, g is sinkward progress divided by 50 m and q is the current estimated MAC success probability; both are dimensionless.','Define observer and relay indexing and distinguish the current link estimate.'),
('• e is remaining','• Candidate energy fraction e is remaining modeled energy divided by 0.5 J; Q is pending-request pressure normalized by 32; R is the dimensionless risk score from Eq. (5). The preselection score S is dimensionless.','Close the dimensional definitions for Eq. (1).'),
('• ℓ is a dimensionless','• For context vector x at observer u and candidate feature vector h for link (u,v), ℓ is a dimensionless action logit. Both feature vectors contain normalized, dimensionless coordinates in the frozen benchmark.','Define feature indexing and dimensions for Eq. (2).'),
('• qθ and kθ','• qθ and kθ are learned query and key transforms; bθ is the learned scalar candidate bias. The symbol qθ denotes a neural transform, whereas q in Eqs. (1) and (4) denotes link success. Parameters θ are fixed during evaluation.','Resolve the overload between neural query notation and link reliability.'),
('Observer u keeps one record','Observer u maintains a separate record for each selected sensor relay v and packet p. Evidence strength s and credited strength c are indexed by that record; effective counts α and β are shared across records for the same observer–relay pair. Each record stores the link-success estimate at registration, ACK status and expiry. A matched overheard forwarding frame contributes strength 0.5 and a reverse receipt generated by sink delivery contributes strength 1.0. Equation (3) retains the maximum, suppressing duplicate credit.','Distinguish packet-specific state from pair-specific effective counts.'),
('• s is the strongest','• s is the strongest matched evidence for record (u,v,p), initialized to 0 and bounded by 1; it is dimensionless.','Specify the initialization and full evidence-record index.'),
('• I_overheard and I_receipt','• I_overheard and I_receipt are dimensionless binary indicators of a matched forwarding-frame event and reverse-receipt event for the same record. Their weights are 0.5 and 1 in Eq. (3).','Define event indicators rather than treating overhearing as proof of reception.'),
('An observation earns credit only','Credit is assigned only when the observer’s own first hop is acknowledged and s exceeds c. Evidence received before the ACK is stored. When that ACK arrives, the same eligibility check applies to the stored evidence. In Eq. (4), q denotes the value cached when record (u,v,p) was registered, rather than a later link estimate. The update is executed only for a strictly positive uncredited increment:','Make the Eq. (4) guard and registration-time convention explicit.'),
('• α is a dimensionless','• α is the dimensionless effective success count for observer–relay pair (u,v), initialized to 1; c is the dimensionless credited strength for record (u,v,p), initialized to 0.','Separate pair-level and packet-level indices in the update.'),
('• q is the dimensionless','• q is the dimensionless cached registration-time link-success estimate. The clip operator limits each positive increment to [0.05, 1]; c is then set to the current s.','Specify clipping bounds, positive-increment guard and credit assignment order.'),
('In the censored arm, the effective failure','In the censored arm, β stays at its initial value of 1 for each observer–relay pair. A failed first hop closes the record without positive credit. For an acknowledged first hop, expiry is set 150 ms after the ACK; absent forwarding evidence causes closure without a failure increment. A later matched observation can still increase s and earn previously unassigned credit. For q<0.1, the 0.05 floor can make two half-credit updates exceed one full q-weighted update. The smallest q in the audited decisions was 0.6923, so this case did not occur in those decisions.','Specify ACK-relative expiry and all late-observation upgrades, consistent with FeedbackLedger.evidence.'),
('Equation (4) applies clipping only','The static floor in Eq. (4) is a heuristic on effective counts, not a Bayesian update. Max-strength deduplication limits the record’s evidence state but does not remove this clipping artifact. In Eq. (5), 1.645 is a fixed multiplier on a beta-form standard deviation; it supplies neither calibrated 95% coverage nor an exact Beta quantile. Changing these rules would define a different feedback mechanism.','Remove repeated caveats while preserving the distinction between evidence state, effective counts and probabilistic coverage.'),
('The policy retains its existing evidence-risk','With the rate-anomaly term disabled, the retained policy maps the pair-specific effective counts to a risk coordinate ρ and an augmented routing score R:','Avoid calling an uncalibrated score a probabilistic mean or confidence bound.'),
('• ρ and R are dimensionless','• ρ and R are dimensionless scores for observer–relay pair (u,v). The factor 0.75 scales both the failure-related coordinate and its uncertainty term; clipping bounds R to [0, 1].','Define the scale and range of Eq. (5).'),
('• σ is the beta-form','• σ = sqrt[αβ / ((α+β)²(α+β+1))] is dimensionless, with α and β taken from the same observer–relay pair. The beta-form expression supplies a score component, not an evaluated posterior interval.','State the variance indexing and limit of its probabilistic interpretation.'),
('For each class, the source updates','For a fixed source and traffic class c, the online service debt is updated once when that source settles a packet. The recurrence follows the virtual-queue form associated with constraint tracking [18]:','Define Eq. (6) as an event-indexed source update, not a physical queue or per-slot recurrence.'),
('• Zc is a dimensionless','• Zc is the dimensionless debt for class c at the fixed source; bc is the dimensionless allowed violation fraction per settled class-c packet. The source index and update-event index are suppressed in Eq. (6).','Make suppressed indices and units explicit.'),
('• I_violation is 1','• I_violation is 1 if no receipt is available by service expiry or receipt age exceeds the class deadline, and 0 otherwise. A separate loss-debt channel uses the analogous receipt/expiry outcome. These online indicators differ from the sink-arrival endpoint in Eq. (8).','Correct the distinction between source-observed receipt age and sink delivery delay.'),
('In this benchmark, only the source updates','Only sources update these debts, on receipt or a 1.5 s expiry; intermediate relays retain no complete debt for transit service. Receipt age includes the reverse path, so a timely sink delivery can still produce a late source-observed outcome. The simulator maintains a shared visited set and reverse-path map without serializing their dissemination. Beacon energy and queue values are likewise supplied as metadata keyed to a transmitted identifier, with access gated by a radio-receive callback. Figure 1 marks these simulator-held inputs. Section 5 evaluates a separate authenticated implementation that decodes transmitted state.','Connect the corrected Eq. (6) definition to the implementation and the Fig. (1) boundary.'),
('Figure 3 traces the experimental stages.','Figure 3 records the source freeze, technical pilot and retained evaluation runs. Telemetry fixtures 76001–76030 informed the redesign. The protocol, source and decision rule were committed as 4027f071322cb5682f39329f656d76df3b68ff62 before fixtures 77001–77030 were evaluated. Technical pilot 76901 is excluded from inference. Each new fixture uses unchanged attention and MLP checkpoints from seed 41001 plus its fixture offset.','Remove redundant pipeline narration while preserving all fixture identifiers and the complete hash.'),
('Under blackholes, censored passive attention delivered','Under blackholes, censored passive attention delivered 75.94% of offered packets, compared with 71.28% for active proofs. The paired gain was 4.67 percentage points (95% CI [2.36, 6.97]; Holm p=0.0161). Figure 4 compares delivery contrasts across settings; Fig. 5 shows the paired blackhole observations and all control contrasts. Among the delivery contrasts, only the blackhole comparison against active proofs survived the 60-test correction. The energy-per-byte contrast also survives correction (Section 4.2).','Prevent a delivery-specific significance statement from being read as excluding the energy-per-byte result.'),
('Under blackholes, energy per delivered payload','Under blackholes, energy per delivered payload byte decreased by 0.0006443 J/byte relative to active proofs (95% CI [−0.0009740, −0.0003145]; Holm p=0.0239). Total modeled sensor radio energy rose from 22.546943 to 22.547473 J, with a mean increase of 0.000531 J computed before rounding. The lower ratio reflects delivery efficiency rather than reduced total energy. Receiving/listening accounts for an average 99.36% of modeled sensor radio energy across the 750 runs.','Explain the rounded energy difference and denominator-driven efficiency gain.'),
('The −1.78-point attention–greedy difference','The −1.78-point attention–greedy difference under selective dropping has an interval that crosses zero. It therefore supports neither attention superiority nor a claim that greedy is better. Replacing the training RSSI proxy with LQI, using raw queue counts and restricting forwarding credit to signed receipts can change the policy’s input distribution; the experiments do not isolate their causal effects. Greedy avoids neural weights and tensor inference, making it a sensible starting point for deployment assessment, although neighbor state, authentication and packet processing still incur costs.','Separate the observed null comparison from causal hypotheses and deployment judgment.'),
('The transfer runs show','The frozen host policies operate on serialized simulated-radio frames with multiple relay choices. For attention, critical-deadline failure is 31.17% in benign runs and 47.83% under selective dropping when undelivered packets count as failures. Total modeled radio energy is approximately 2.519 and 2.520 J per six-node run. Always-on listening and repeated authenticated telemetry dominate this radio-only account; embedded CPU and cryptographic energy are excluded.','Consolidate repeated non-superiority statements and retain all system-cost boundaries.'),
('The full actor–critic contains 63,368','The inference actor contains 44,161 parameters, requiring 176,644 FP32 weight bytes before runtime buffers; the full actor–critic contains 63,368 parameters. Removing training-only heads therefore changes the storage estimate, but neither count establishes target feasibility. Duty-cycled MAC performance, drift tolerance, target inference and measured energy require separate validation.','State the actor-only resource result directly without conversational reference to correcting a review.'),
('The main result concerns replacement','The benchmark supports replacing the tested active-proof mechanism within its prespecified margins. Because eligibility and expiry rules change together with control traffic, the observed difference cannot be assigned to proof airtime alone. Comparisons with naive passive and frozen prior do not establish a unique censoring effect after correction. Retaining the earlier unsuccessful architecture comparisons prevents the feedback result from being recast as evidence for neural-policy superiority.','Make the contribution and attribution limits explicit in one compact argument.'),
('The holdout fixes passive strength','The holdout fixes passive strength at 0.5, record expiry at 150 ms, cache life at 0.75 s, the current model and all inference checkpoints. Section 5.5 varies the preselection coefficients only; sensitivity to these other choices remains unknown. Changes to serialization, ACK authentication, service tracking or ledger retirement require a separately frozen experiment because they change the evaluated mechanism.','Reconcile the sensitivity limitation with the new coefficient experiment.'),
('Receipt-assisted passive feedback passed','ACK-gated censored passive feedback passed the prespecified replacement test on 30 new fixtures, improving blackhole delivery over active proofs by 4.67 percentage points. The matched controls establish neither a unique censoring effect nor an attention advantage. In the separate 180-run authenticated transport study, frozen policies operate on received wire state and local service records without an established attention benefit. Serial-interface testing corrected a receive-time error, and four emulated Cortex-M3 boards execute the compiled UART-to-radio bridge while inference and cryptography remain on the host. The 60–300 s extension exposes routing-energy exhaustion and increasing source debt. Together, these results define the benchmark’s supported feedback comparison and deployment boundary: absolute service compliance, physical-board operation, embedded policy/crypto execution and measured energy remain unvalidated.','Close on the supported contribution, null controls and host/MCU boundary without implying sustained deployment.')]

ALGORITHM=[
(0,'For each received event or 1 ms polling tick:'),
(1,'If a routing request is pending:'),
(2,'Reject visited/exhausted nodes and the 22-hop cap; form at most eight candidates.'),
(2,'If none is feasible, stop this request; otherwise select the masked-policy argmax.'),
(2,'For a non-sink relay, register (u,v,p) and cache q at registration; transmit DATA.'),
(1,'Else if the event is the observer’s own first-hop MAC result:'),
(2,'On success, mark ACK eligibility and set expiry to ACK time + 150 ms.'),
(2,'On failure, close the record without incrementing α or β.'),
(1,'Else if matched forwarding evidence or a reverse receipt is received:'),
(2,'Ignore unknown records and closed records without a successful own ACK.'),
(2,'Update the strongest evidence s by Eq. (3), retaining any earlier stronger value.'),
(1,'After either a successful ACK or an accepted evidence event:'),
(2,'If ACK-eligible and s > c, apply Eq. (4); then set credited strength c to s.'),
(1,'At each polling tick, close expired records without a β increment.'),
(2,'Retain acknowledged records so later matched evidence can upgrade s and c.'),
(1,'At a source receipt or 1.5 s service expiry, if the packet is unsettled:'),
(2,'Update its class debt once by Eq. (6), then mark the packet settled.')]

def apply(doc,root,write_report=True):
 changes=[]
 for prefix,new,reason in EDITS:
  matches=[p for p in doc.paragraphs if p.text.startswith(prefix)]
  if len(matches)!=1:raise ValueError('Editorial anchor not unique: '+prefix)
  p=matches[0];old=p.text;p.text=new;changes.append(dict(before=old,after=new,reason=reason))
 # Replace the flat list with an explicitly scoped, nested event procedure.
 ps=doc.paragraphs;head=next(p for p in ps if p.text.startswith('Algorithm 1:'));i=ps.index(head) if head in ps else next(i for i,p in enumerate(ps) if p._p is head._p)
 # Paragraph wrapper identity is not stable across doc.paragraphs calls.
 i=next(i for i,p in enumerate(ps) if p._p is head._p)
 end=next(i2 for i2 in range(i+1,len(ps)) if ps[i2]._p.find('.//'+__import__('docx').oxml.ns.qn('w:drawing')) is not None)
 for p in ps[i+1:end]:p._p.getparent().remove(p._p)
 from docx.oxml import OxmlElement
 from docx.text.paragraph import Paragraph
 previous=head
 head.text='Algorithm 1: ACK-gated censored passive routing';head.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.LEFT
 lines=[(0,'Input: radio events, cached telemetry, fixed policy θ; censored mode, 150 ms timeout.'),(0,'Output: next-hop requests, observer evidence and source-service debts.')]+[(level,f'{n:02d}.  '+text) for n,(level,text) in enumerate(ALGORITHM,1)]
 for k,(level,text) in enumerate(lines):
  el=OxmlElement('w:p');previous._p.addnext(el);p=Paragraph(el,head._parent);p.text=text;p.alignment=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.LEFT
  p.paragraph_format.left_indent=Cm(.55+level*.5);p.paragraph_format.first_line_indent=Cm(-.55 if k>=2 else -.55)
  p.paragraph_format.space_before=Pt(0);p.paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(1);p.paragraph_format.line_spacing=1.05;p.paragraph_format.keep_with_next=k<len(lines)-1;p.paragraph_format.keep_together=True
  for r in p.runs:r.font.name='Times New Roman';r.font.size=Pt(9.5)
  previous=p
 head.paragraph_format.keep_with_next=True
 # Scope the body reference so active and naive controls are not misread as this procedure.
 p=next(p for p in doc.paragraphs if p.text.startswith('Algorithm 1 gives'))
 old=p.text;p.text='Algorithm 1 gives the censored-passive event procedure; Table 3 specifies the other arms. Figure 2 shows the ACK gate and strongest-evidence lifecycle. Radio callback controls check reception of a two-hop forwarding observation, absence of reception at an out-of-range observer and absence of proof frames in the passive arm. They test callback paths rather than authentication or intrusion-classification accuracy.'
 changes.append(dict(before=old,after=p.text,reason='Explicitly scope the algorithm to the censored arm and separate the Table 3 controls.'))
 # Correct the context description without altering feature dimensions or data.
 p=next(p for p in doc.paragraphs if p.text.startswith('The observation contains 13 context'))
 old=p.text;p.text=p.text.replace('six source-service debts','six node-local service-debt coordinates, updated only at sources in this benchmark');changes.append(dict(before=old,after=p.text,reason='Do not imply that intermediate relays receive an updated source-debt vector.'))
 if write_report:(root/'publication/array/editorial_changes.json').write_text(json.dumps(changes,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
 return changes
